{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1390039-mokole-in-the-water-hazard","id":1390039,"title":"Mokole in the water hazard?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-19T12:57:02-07:00","id":1390039,"title":"Mokole in the water hazard?","content":"So as a rather odd question related to an adventure I'm trying to write. Is there any proper reason a crocodile like mokole would be dwelling in a former most turned golf course water hazard? Ask away if you need me to be more specific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T13:07:42-07:00","id":1390045,"title":"","content":"Well just to acknowledge the setting for a moment, the Mokol\u00e9 are, alongside the Nuwishu and Gurahl, probably some of the least common changing breeds still active.<br /> <br /> That set aside, the Mokol\u00e9 can really settle down anywhere they can establish a spiritual territory (I forget their name for them, but it's similar yet distinct to a Bastet Den-Realm), although most are found residing around one of the Rivers of Memory (or some such make, I haven't read the Mokol\u00e9 breed book in some time) to maintain better access to the Primordial Memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T13:18:11-07:00","id":1390049,"title":"","content":"I'll look into that. But at least I have a direction I think. Now a bit more odd is I'm trying to come up with a good reason for that place to have a few golf balls that fall in there turn into minor magical items that protect against dangers at sea, such as drowning or predators... It's related to a type of magical amulet from Philippine myth called a &quot;crocodile pearl&quot;. Lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T13:19:36-07:00","id":1390050,"title":"","content":"One could argue that if the golf balls landed near or within the Mokol\u00e9's spiritual domain, they might have been suffused with some ambient gnosis and become talons with that sort of effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T13:57:18-07:00","id":1390055,"title":"","content":"I suppose. Lol. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T14:29:33-07:00","id":1390065,"title":"","content":"Golf balls falling into the crocodile's realm could easily be explained as 'feeding the crocodile.' I mean there's an alligator in Happy Gilmore, an Adam Sandler movie, that eats golf balls hit into its area (and humans).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T14:33:37-07:00","id":1390066,"title":"","content":"Alligators actually are frequent pests at golf courses along the Gulf of Mexico coast, especially in Florida and Alabama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T14:57:56-07:00","id":1390072,"title":"","content":"That and the idea of a &quot;crocodile pearl&quot; golf ball is what made me think of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T16:14:16-07:00","id":1390403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1390039-mokole-in-the-water-hazard?p=1390045#post1390045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well just to acknowledge the setting for a moment, the Mokol\u00e9 are, alongside the Nuwishu and Gurahl, probably some of the least common changing breeds still active.<br /> <br /> That set aside, the Mokol\u00e9 can really settle down anywhere they can establish a spiritual territory (I forget their name for them, but it's similar yet distinct to a Bastet Den-Realm), although most are found residing around one of the Rivers of Memory (or some such make, I haven't read the Mokol\u00e9 breed book in some time) to maintain better access to the Primordial Memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mokole became more common in Revised and on, per the writeups they boasted in various Changing Breeds books. As for their Wallows, they've typically been likened more to caerns than Den-Realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https:/